  "decision": "no_change",
  "headline": "Custom ramps constrain capture, but no added Q4 substitution is established; hold NVIDIA $371.43bn and fiscal Q4 $127bn",
  "note": "I partly agree with the challenge: custom ramps are real. AWS reported Trainium3 production workloads and expected supply commitments by mid-2026, but that does not date October–December hardware purchases or identify NVIDIA substitution [amzn-2026-02-05-release]. April’s chip counts and July’s chips revenue cannot supply hardware-dollar shares [amzn-2026-04-29-release] [amzn-2026-07-30-release].\n\nAlphabet’s external TPU agreements began revenue recognition in Q2, with most expected in 2027; they do not reveal Google’s internal TPU procurement. NVIDIA separately names Google Cloud Rubin racks and AWS planned deployment [web-fb40041ca0] [nvda-2026-08-26-release] [nvda-2026-02-25-release]. These relationships establish exposure, not contracted share.\n\nThe channel’s custom-share signal concerns unnamed 2027 orders. Its dated 2026 slip describes deferral, already reflected in our $3.19bn allowance, rather than custom replacement [channel-oct2026] [channel-q4-slip]. Refreshed SEC indices and later filings added no procurement schedule; IR pages did not yield usable transcripts.\n\nCompute shows 65%→64% alone cuts NVIDIA $5.71bn. Pairing concentration to preserve outside-customer revenue instead cuts $2.55bn to $368.88bn. This is an illustrative additional cohort loss, not evidence or a forecast change.\n\nI hold 65% base share, Q3 $102bn and fiscal Q4 $127bn. Calendar Q4 is October–December; fiscal Q4 includes January. Move on dated, net substitution dollars beyond existing allowances. NVIDIA’s long earnings case is unchanged here: $371.43bn base remains $4.57bn below street (-1.22%).",
  "stance": "Capex exceeds street, but deployment timing weakens NVIDIA’s calendar capture; current custom ramps do not establish another Q4 revenue loss.",
  "rationale": "Partly agree with the analyst’s structural custom-risk challenge; do not infer another calendar-Q4 cut from previously considered capacity, unit and revenue disclosures. The existing split, custom-risk bull adjustment and $3.19bn dated-slip allowance remain judgments. Further cohort losses require concentration reconciliation, current recognition dates and overlap adjustment. No new guidance or procurement fact shifts the 2026 odds enough to justify an additional input or quarterly change.",
  "thesis": "Calendar-2026 capex remains $682.5bn versus $667.5bn street. NVIDIA bear/base/bull $343.79bn/$371.43bn/$391.79bn versus $376bn; base deficit $4.57bn (-1.22%). Hold base mix 37.3%, NVIDIA split 65%, concentration 44.55%; AMD GPU base approximately$14bn. Hold unreported NVIDIA Q3 DC$102bn and own fiscal Q4$127bn versus required$126.58bn. Internal Google procurement, AWS hardware dollars and additional recognized substitution in Oct-Dec remain unresolved; external TPU sales and January require separate customer/period mapping.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "statement": "AWS reported Trainium3 production workloads and expected supply commitments by mid-2026; this is not a Q4 delivery schedule.",
      "entities": [
        "AMZN"
      ],
      "claim_period": "February 5, 2026 disclosure",
      "citation": {
        "source_id": "amzn-2026-02-05-release",
        "quote": "Trainium3 is now delivering production workloads and seeing strong demand, with nearly all Trainium3 supply of chips expected to be committed by mid-2026."
      }
    },
    {
      "statement": "AWS reported landed/subscribed Trainium2 capacity; chip counts and inference use do not establish spend share.",
      "entities": [
        "AMZN"
      ],
      "claim_period": "February 5, 2026 disclosure",
      "citation": {
        "source_id": "amzn-2026-02-05-release",
        "quote": "Trainium2 is fully subscribed with 1.4 million chips landed, and powers the majority of inference on Bedrock, a service used by 100,000+ companies."
      }
    },
    {
      "statement": "Trainium4 delivery was expected to begin in 2027, rather than establishing a calendar-Q4 2026 ramp.",
      "entities": [
        "AMZN"
      ],
      "claim_period": "February 5, 2026 outlook for 2027",
      "citation": {
        "source_id": "amzn-2026-02-05-release",
        "quote": "Trainium4 is expected to start delivering in 2027, with 6 times the FP4 compute performance, 4 times more memory bandwidth, and 2 times more high memory bandwidth capacity than Trainium3."
      }
    },
    {
      "statement": "External TPU sales began recognition in Q2 with most expected in 2027; this does not establish Google internal procurement.",
      "entities": [
        "GOOGL"
      ],
      "claim_period": "Q2 2026 filing; expected 2027 revenue",
      "citation": {
        "source_id": "web-fb40041ca0",
        "quote": "We have signed a limited number of agreements to supply TPU systems to customers who require or provide on-premises infrastructure for specialized, high-scale workloads. In the second quarter of 2026, we began recognizing revenues from these agreements, with the significant majority to be recognized in 2027."
      }
    },
    {
      "statement": "The channel gives no quantified custom share or named customer identities.",
      "entities": [
        "MSFT",
        "GOOGL",
        "META",
        "AMZN",
        "NVDA"
      ],
      "claim_period": "October 1–8, 2026 interviews about forward orders",
      "citation": {
        "source_id": "channel-oct2026",
        "quote": "Two respondents said custom accelerators are a rising share of new rack orders at two of the four largest US clouds; neither would quantify it."
      }
    },
    {
      "statement": "The dated-slip report describes deferral, not a measured custom replacement of NVIDIA purchases.",
      "entities": [
        "NVDA",
        "AMD"
      ],
      "claim_period": "October 9–12, 2026 interviews",
      "citation": {
        "source_id": "channel-q4-slip",
        "quote": "They described the orders as deferred, not cancelled."
      }
    }
  ],
  "capex_changes": [],
  "changes": [],
  "implications": [
    {
      "company": "NVDA",
      "customer": "AMZN",
      "relationship_id": "aws-nvda",
      "interpretation": "February 25 Rubin partnership and April29 planned NVIDIA deployment establish dated AWS exposure alongside Trainium growth.",
      "uncertainty": "No October–December NVIDIA invoice value, acceptance dates or counterfactual replacement orders are disclosed. AWS is not assigned any portion of the anonymous dated slip.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_id": "nvda-2026-02-25-release",
          "quote": "cloud providers Amazon Web Services (AWS), Google Cloud, Microsoft Azure and Oracle Cloud Infrastructure will be among the first to deploy Vera Rubin-based instances."
        },
        {
          "source_id": "amzn-2026-04-29-release",
          "quote": "Landed 2.1 million+ AI chips over the past 12 months, more than half of which were Trainium, and announced one million+ NVIDIA GPUs to be deployed starting in 2026, giving customers the widest range of accelerated compute options."
        },
        {
          "source_id": "amzn-2026-02-05-release",
          "quote": "Trainium3 is now delivering production workloads and seeing strong demand, with nearly all Trainium3 supply of chips expected to be committed by mid-2026."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "company": "NVDA",
      "customer": "GOOGL",
      "relationship_id": "gcp-nvda",
      "interpretation": "May 20 A5X/Blackwell collaboration and August 26 Rubin racks at Google Cloud establish a current supplier/customer relationship alongside TPU offerings.",
      "uncertainty": "Relationships do not establish procurement shares. External TPU buyers can be outside the modeled four, requiring a different concentration allocation; no anonymous deferred order is assigned to Google.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_id": "nvda-2026-05-20-release",
          "quote": "Expanded collaboration with Google Cloud to advance agentic and physical AI, including new NVIDIA Vera Rubin-powered A5X instances and a preview of Google Gemini models on Google Distributed Cloud running on NVIDIA Blackwell and Blackwell Ultra GPUs."
        },
        {
          "source_id": "nvda-2026-08-26-release",
          "quote": "Announced the NVIDIA Vera Rubin platform is ramping into full production with racks running at partners including CoreWeave, Google Cloud, Microsoft Azure, Oracle Cloud Infrastructure and Nebius."
        },
        {
          "source_id": "web-fb40041ca0",
          "quote": "We have signed a limited number of agreements to supply TPU systems to customers who require or provide on-premises infrastructure for specialized, high-scale workloads. In the second quarter of 2026, we began recognizing revenues from these agreements, with the significant majority to be recognized in 2027."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "No dated internal Google TPU/NVIDIA procurement-dollar split or AWS Q4 hardware invoice schedule is available in reviewed evidence.",
    "Custom deployments may expand aggregate capacity, substitute prior NVIDIA plans, or do both; no net counterfactual is quantified.",
    "External TPU revenue is neither Google own PP&E nor necessarily Big-Four customer spend; minority recognition in 2026 is possible but unquantified.",
    "Annual-average share stress is not Q4 share. October affects NVIDIA fiscal Q3; January affects fiscal Q4/calendar2027.",
    "The existing timing allowance and new substitution hypothesis may refer to the same orders; matched losses must be reconciled rather than added twice.",
    "Paired-concentration sensitivities assume loss inside the modeled four and unchanged outside revenue, conditions not established for external TPU displacement.",
    "IR pages returned navigation shells or404; absence of a usable transcript does not prove absence of guidance. Later reviewed8Ks concern financing/directors."
  ],
  "catalysts": [
    "Late October 2026: Google internal equipment mix and AWS hardware procurement, named replacement orders and current guidance.",
    "November 18,2026, expected/unconfirmed: NVIDIA Q3 DC versus 102 and fiscal Q4 guide versus own 127/required 126.58, with control-transfer timing.",
    "January 2027: deferred receipts, distinguishing fiscal Q4 revenue from calendar2026 and substitution from rollover.",
    "January–February 2027: custom/total accelerator budgets and values for disclosed Trainium/TPU plans."
  ],
  "disconfirming_evidence": [
    "AWS Trainium3 was already delivering production workloads during 2026, making current custom capture a real risk.",
    "AWS announced NVIDIA deployments and Google Cloud hosts Rubin racks; coexistence does not establish zero substitution.",
    "The external TPU agreements already generated someQ2 revenue; a2027 majority does not imply zero2026 competition.",
    "The channel describes deferred rather than cancelled orders; existing timing risk cannot be counted again as permanent substitution.",
    "A named, net October–December replacement of previously planned NVIDIA invoices would make the held 65% share and 127 fiscal Q4 view too high."
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "source_id": "amzn-2026-04-29-release",
      "quote": "Exceeded $20 billion annual revenue run rate for Amazon’s chips business—inclusive of Graviton, Trainium, and Nitro—which is growing triple-digit percentages year-over-year."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "amzn-2026-07-30-release",
      "quote": "Exceeded a $25 billion annual revenue run rate for its chips business, growing triple-digit percentages year-over-year."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "amzn-2026-04-29-release",
      "quote": "Secured a commitment from OpenAI to consume approximately two gigawatts (GW) of Trainium capacity through AWS infrastructure to power its frontier models and advanced workloads, which begins ramping in 2027."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "web-fb40041ca0",
      "quote": "In 2026, we expect to significantly increase, relative to 2025, our investment in our technical infrastructure, including servers and network equipment and data centers."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "web-b93e425ae9",
      "quote": "Revenue from product sales is recognized upon transfer of control of products to customers in an amount that reflects the consideration we expect to receive in exchange for those products."
    },
    {
